  { "id": "arc-exact", "front": "(HL) Evaluate $\\arcsin\\frac12$, $\\arccos\\left(-\\frac12\\right)$, $\\arctan(-1)$.", "back": "$\\frac\\pi6$, $\\frac{2\\pi}3$, $-\\frac\\pi4$ (each within its principal range).", "concept": "Inverse trig", "kind": "application" },
  { "id": "arc-domains", "front": "(HL) Domains of $\\arcsin$, $\\arccos$, $\\arctan$?", "back": "$\\arcsin, \\arccos$: $-1 \\le x \\le 1$. $\\arctan$: all real $x$.", "concept": "Inverse trig", "kind": "condition" },
  { "id": "arc-composition", "front": "(HL) Is $\\arcsin\\left(\\sin\\frac{5\\pi}6\\right) = \\frac{5\\pi}6$?", "back": "No — $\\arcsin$ returns a value in $\\left[-\\frac\\pi2, \\frac\\pi2\\right]$: the answer is $\\frac\\pi6$. ($\\sin(\\arcsin x) = x$ does hold for $|x| \\le 1$.)", "concept": "Inverse trig", "kind": "misconception" },
  { "id": "arctan-graph", "front": "(HL) Key features of $y = \\arctan x$?", "back": "Domain $\\mathbb R$; increasing, odd; horizontal asymptotes $y = \\pm\\frac\\pi2$; passes through the origin.", "concept": "Inverse trig", "kind": "graph" },
